    "title": "<p>Clinical features of conditions associated with germline predisposition</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Christian P. Kratz",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"margin-left: -.25pt; border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" width=\"931\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 27.05pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 114.0pt; border: none; border-top: solid black 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 27.05pt;\" width=\"152\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Disorder</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 86.75pt; border: none; border-top: solid black 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 27.05pt;\" width=\"116\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Pathogenesis</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.1pt; border: none; border-top: solid black 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 27.05pt;\" width=\"119\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Inheritance pattern</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 67.95pt; border: none; border-top: solid black 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 27.05pt;\" width=\"91\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Genes</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 110.25pt; border: none; border-top: solid black 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 27.05pt;\" width=\"147\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Age of onset of myeloid neoplasm</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 230.15pt; border: none; border-top: solid black 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 27.05pt;\" width=\"307\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 31.35pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 114.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 31.35pt;\" width=\"152\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><em>ANKRD26</em>-related thrombocytopenia</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 86.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 31.35pt;\" width=\"116\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Altered MAPK signalling</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 31.35pt;\" width=\"119\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Inherited, heterozygous</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 67.95pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 31.35pt;\" width=\"91\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>ANKRD26</em></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 110.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 31.35pt;\" width=\"147\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Adulthood &gt; childhood</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 230.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 31.35pt;\" width=\"307\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>No syndromic features</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Thrombocytopenia</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Variable platelet function abnormalities</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 39.55pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 114.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 39.55pt;\" width=\"152\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><em>CBL</em> syndrome</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 86.75pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 39.55pt;\" width=\"116\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Impaired degradation of cell-surface receptors, dysregulated RAS pathway signalling</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.1pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 39.55pt;\" width=\"119\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Inherited or de&nbsp;novo, heterozygous</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 67.95pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 39.55pt;\" width=\"91\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>CBL</em></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 110.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 39.55pt;\" width=\"147\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Early childhood</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 230.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 39.55pt;\" width=\"307\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Juvenile myelomonocytic leukaemia</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Noonan syndrome&ndash;like disorder: facial dysmorphism, cardiac disease, musculoskeletal anomalies, cognitive deficits</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Vasculopathy</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Variable syndrome expressivity</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 39.55pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 114.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 39.55pt;\" width=\"152\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><em>CEBPA</em>-associated familial AML</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 86.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 39.55pt;\" width=\"116\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Altered transcriptional regulation</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 39.55pt;\" width=\"119\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Inherited, heterozygous</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 67.95pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 39.55pt;\" width=\"91\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>CEBPA</em></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 110.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 39.55pt;\" width=\"147\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Childhood, adulthood</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 230.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 39.55pt;\" width=\"307\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>No syndromic features</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 14.45pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 114.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"152\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Familial platelet disorder with associated myeloid malignancy</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 86.75pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"116\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Altered transcriptional regulation</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.1pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"119\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Inherited, heterozygous</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 67.95pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"91\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>RUNX1</em></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 110.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"147\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Adulthood &gt; childhood</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 230.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"307\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Variable thrombocytopenia with increased bleeding risk, rarely T-ALL</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 14.45pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 114.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"152\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Fanconi anaemia</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 86.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"116\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Impaired Fanconi pathway of interstrand crosslink DNA repair</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"119\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Inherited, homozygous, compound heterozygous, or X-linked (FANCB) or heterozygous (FANCR)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 67.95pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"91\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&gt;&nbsp;22&nbsp;genes (<em>FANCA</em>, <em>FANCC</em>, <em>FANCG</em> most common)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 110.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"147\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Childhood, adulthood</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 230.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"307\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Congenital malformations, facial dysmorphism</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Bone marrow failure</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Squamous cell carcinomas and liver tumours</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Sensitivity to genotoxic agents</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 14.45pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 114.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"152\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><em>GATA2</em> haploinsufficiency syndromes</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 86.75pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"116\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Altered transcriptional regulation</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.1pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"119\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Inherited, heterozygous</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 67.95pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"91\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>GATA2</em></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 110.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"147\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Late childhood, early adulthood</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 230.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"307\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>May occur as non-syndromic MDS associated with monosomy&nbsp;7 or trisomy&nbsp;8</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Bone marrow failure or neutropenia</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Severe immunodeficiencies: monocytopenia, dendritic cell deficiency, or lymphocyte deficiency</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Mycobacterial infections</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Monocytopenia and mycobacterial infection (MonoMAC) syndrome</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Pulmonary alveolar proteinosis</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Emberger syndrome: lymphoedema</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 14.45pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 114.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"152\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Neurofibromatosis type&nbsp;1</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 86.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"116\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Aberrant RAS pathway signalling</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"119\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Inherited</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 67.95pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"91\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>NF1</em></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 110.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"147\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Early childhood</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 230.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"307\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"FR\">Features include caf&eacute;-au-lait spots, neurofibromas</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Noonan syndrome&ndash;like disorder</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Non-myeloid tumours</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Variable syndrome expressivity</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 14.45pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 114.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"152\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><em>SAMD9</em>-related syndromes</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 86.75pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"116\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Altered cellular proliferation pathways</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.1pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"119\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">De&nbsp;novo, heterozygous</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 67.95pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"91\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>SAMD9</em></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 110.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"147\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Early childhood</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 230.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"307\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>MIRAGE syndrome (myelodysplasia, infection, restriction of growth, adrenal hypoplasia, genital phenotypes, and enteropathy)</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>May occur as non-syndromic monosomy&nbsp;7 MDS or bone marrow failure</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 14.45pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 114.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"152\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><em>SAMD9L</em>-related syndromes</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 86.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"116\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Altered cellular proliferation pathways</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"119\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Inherited or de&nbsp;novo, heterozygous</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 67.95pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"91\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>SAMD9L</em></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 110.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"147\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Early childhood</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 230.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"307\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Ataxia-pancytopenia syndrome</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>May occur as non-syndromic monosomy&nbsp;7 MDS or bone marrow failure</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 14.45pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 114.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"152\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Severe congenital neutropenia</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 86.75pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"116\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>ELANE</em>: endoplasmic reticulum stress, promyelocyte apoptosis</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.1pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"119\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Inherited or de&nbsp;novo, heterozygous</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 67.95pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"91\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&gt;&nbsp;10&nbsp;genes (<em>ELANE</em> most common)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 110.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"147\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Childhood, adulthood</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 230.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"307\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Severe bacterial infections</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Neutropenia</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>G-CSF dependence</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 14.45pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 114.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"152\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Shwachman&ndash;Diamond syndrome</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 86.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"116\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Impaired ribosome assembly</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"119\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Inherited, homozygous or compound heterozygous (for <em>SBDS</em>)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 67.95pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"91\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>SBDS</em> (&gt;&nbsp;90%), <em>EFL1</em>, <em>DNAJC21</em>, <em>SRP54</em></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 110.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"147\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Childhood, adulthood</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 230.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 14.45pt;\" width=\"307\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Exocrine pancreatic dysfunction</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Variable cytopenias</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Skeletal dysplasia</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Hepatomegaly and transaminitis in early childhood</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>May occur as non-syndromic aplastic anaemia or MDS/AML</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 141.5pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 114.0pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid black 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 141.5pt;\" width=\"152\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Telomere biology disorders</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 86.75pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid black 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 141.5pt;\" width=\"116\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Impaired telomere maintenance</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.1pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid black 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 141.5pt;\" width=\"119\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Inherited or de&nbsp;novo, heterozygous, homozygous, compound heterozygous, X-linked hemizygous</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 67.95pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid black 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 141.5pt;\" width=\"91\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&gt;&nbsp;12&nbsp;genes (<em>DKC1</em>, <em>TERC</em>, <em>TERT</em>, <em>TINF2</em> most common)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 110.25pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid black 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 141.5pt;\" width=\"147\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Late childhood, adulthood</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 230.15pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid black 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 141.5pt;\" width=\"307\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Dyskeratosis congenita: mucocutaneous triad of nail/hair abnormalities, skin rash, and leukoplakia</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Bone marrow failure</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Pulmonary fibrosis</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Liver cirrhosis</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Vascular anomalies</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>May occur as non-syndromic aplastic anaemia or monosomy&nbsp;7 MDS</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">AML, acute myeloid leukaemia; MDS, myelodysplastic syndrome; T-ALL, T-lymphoblastic leukaemia.</p>",
